<div class="table-wrap surface-roles">
  <table>
    <caption>Three places for your course work</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">What it does not own</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Canvas and its calendar</strong> Due dates, submissions, feedback, grades, and official course operations.</td>
        <td>The complete teaching path or your source files.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Course site</strong> Welcome, syllabus, lessons, tutorials, shared story, examples, practice, and onward routes.</td>
        <td>The authoritative gradebook, production identity, or unapproved student records.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Your repository</strong> Source work, project history, revisions, and the workspace that grows toward your portfolio.</td>
        <td>Official deadlines, grades, or private institutional records.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
